        "original_id": "e4e70e92-a8ab-53ba-a083-1807997dd91e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. P. Doherty, Debbie Harry, Cyndi Lauper\n- Music Works: \"Maybe for Sure\", \"Necessary Evil\", Def, Dumb & Blonde\n- Events: True Colors tour, Necessary Evil tour\n- Bands: Blondie\n\nFacts:\n- Debbie Harry was born Deborah Ann Harry, née Angela Tremble, on July 1, 1945.\n- Debbie Harry is an American singer-songwriter and actress best known as the lead singer of Blondie.\n- \"Maybe for Sure\" is a 1989 song by Debbie Harry.\n- \"Maybe for Sure\" was released as a single from Debbie Harry's third solo album Def, Dumb & Blonde.\n- In June 2007, J. P. Doherty toured with Debbie Harry on Cyndi Lauper's True Colors tour.\n- In November and December 2007, J. P. Doherty toured with Debbie Harry on the Necessary Evil tour.\n- The Necessary Evil tour supported Debbie Harry's 2007 release Necessary Evil.",
